diting platform for the rice leaffolder, Cnaphalocrocis medinalis.","authorString":"Yan J, Liu B, Lu H, Zhan S, Chen D, Xu J.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Yan J","lastName":"Yan","firstName":"Juncheng","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Plant Trait Design, Center for Excellence in Molecular Plant Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."},{"affiliation":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Liu B","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Bingpeng","initials":"B","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Plant Trait Design, Center for Excellence in Molecular Plant Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Lu H","lastName":"Lu","firstName":"Hui","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Plant Trait Design, Center for Excellence in Molecular Plant Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhan S","lastName":"Zhan","firstName":"Shuai","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Plant Trait Design, Center for Excellence in Molecular Plant Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Chen D","lastName":"Chen","firstName":"Dongbin","initials":"D","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Plant Trait Design, Center for Excellence in Molecular Plant Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Xu J","lastName":"Xu","firstName":"Jun","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7963-0253"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Plant Trait Design, Center for Excellence in Molecular Plant Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7963-0253"}]},"journalInfo":{"journalIssueId":4252797,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Insect Sci","title":"Insect science","essn":"1744-7917","issn":"1672-9609","nlmid":"101266965","isoabbreviation":"Insect Sci"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-09-01"},"pubYear":"2026","abstractText":"A CRISPR/Cas9 toolkit was established for the rice leaffolder (Cnaphalocrocis medinalis) using entirely endogenous regulatory elements. An all-in-one plasmid was constructed containing an IE1-EGFP marker, a CmU6 promoter driven sgRNA targeting Cmebony, and a Cmactin5C promoter driven Cas9. This platform provides a system for functional genomics in this pest.","affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Plant Trait Design, Center for Excellence in Molecular Plant Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Shanghai, China.","publicationStatus":"aheadofprint","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Letter"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"CAS Pioneer Hundred Talents Program","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Center for Excellence in Molecular Plant Sciences","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","orderIn":0}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1744-7917.70360"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCreation":"2026-09-11","dateOfRevision":"2026-09-11","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-09-10","firstPublicationDate":"2026-09-10","firstIndexDate":"2026-09-11","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42747567","source":"MED","pmid":"42747567","pmcid":"PMC13582722","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13582722"]},"doi":"10.1007/s00253-026-14030-6","title":"An inducer-independent, single-plasmid CRISPR-Cas9 system for genome editing in Bacillus species.","authorString":"Hilkmann M, Welsch N, Felle MF, Schweder T, Appelbaum M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Hilkmann M","lastName":"Hilkmann","firstName":"Maximilian","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Marine Biotechnology, 17489, Greifswald, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Welsch N","lastName":"Welsch","firstName":"Norma","initials":"N","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Marine Biotechnology, 17489, Greifswald, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Felle MF","lastName":"Felle","firstName":"Max Fabian","initials":"MF","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"BASF SE, 67063, Ludwigshafen Am Rhein, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Schweder T","lastName":"Schweder","firstName":"Thomas","initials":"T","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7213-3596"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany. schweder@uni-greifswald.de."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Marine Biotechnology, 17489, Greifswald, Germany. schweder@uni-greifswald.de."}]}},{"fullName":"Appelbaum M","lastName":"Appelbaum","firstName":"Mathis","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany. mathis.appelbaum@basf.com."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Marine Biotechnology, 17489, Greifswald, Germany. mathis.appelbaum@basf.com."},{"affiliation":"BASF SE, 67063, Ludwigshafen Am Rhein, Germany. mathis.appelbaum@basf.com."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7213-3596"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"110","journalIssueId":4261033,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Appl Microbiol Biotechnol","title":"Applied microbiology and biotechnology","essn":"1432-0614","issn":"0175-7598","nlmid":"8406612","isoabbreviation":"Appl Microbiol Biotechnol"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-09-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"278","abstractText":"Advances in molecular biology tools are essential for streamlining and accelerating genetic engineering of cells across industrial and academic applications. While CRISPR-Cas improves genome editing efficiency, current systems have limitations and are often host specific, which restricts their versatility. This study describes a versatile CRISPR-Cas9 system for genome editing in industrially relevant Bacillus species. By adapting the well-established pJOE8999 vector-based CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing system, we constructed an inducer-independent, broad-host-range genome editing system. It maintains the benefits of low toxicity to the target cell and the cloning host as well as the ease to use of a single-plasmid CRISPR-Cas9 system. We utilized the constitutive Sigma70-type promoter from the conserved veg gene of Bacillus, to develop and test the suitability of promoter variants of different strengths for Cas9 expression. Successful gene deletions in three different Bacillus species demonstrated the versatility of the modified system for this industrially important genus. This was further confirmed by the integration of a reporter gene fusion and the introduction of a single point mutation in the genome of Bacillus licheniformis. This one-step CRISPR-based transformation protocol developed in this study enables fast genome editing workflows with minimal hands-on time. KEY POINTS: • Editing and screening of promoter variants for balanced Cas9 expression in Bacillus. • Development of a versatile inducer-independent, single-plasmid CRISPR-Cas-based system. • Verification of the modified CRISPR-based system for genome editing in different Bacilli.","affiliation":"Pharmaceutical Biotechnology, Institute of Pharmacy, University of Greifswald, 17487, Greifswald, Germany.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Universität Greifswald","orderIn":0},{"agency":"BASF","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Bacillus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Gene Deletion"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genome, Bacterial"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Plasmids","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Promoter Regions, Genetic"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Editing","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Bacillus","Promoter","Genome Editing","Crispr-cas","Strain Optimization"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00253-026-14030-6"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13582722"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13582722?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["gen","refseq"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-09-16","dateOfCreation":"2026-09-16","dateOfRevision":"2026-09-24","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-09-11","firstPublicationDate":"2026-09-11","firstIndexDate":"2026-09-17","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-09-25","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"PPR1325806","source":"PPR","doi":"10.21203/rs.3.rs-10919496/v1","title":"CRISPR/Cas9-mediated multicopy δ-site integration in Saccharomyces cerevisiae via Cas9 expression","authorString":"Pidkurhanna O, Tigunova O, Shulga S.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Pidkurhanna O","lastName":"Pidkurhanna","firstName":"Oleksandra","initials":"O"},{"fullName":"Tigunova O","lastName":"Tigunova","firstName":"Olena","initials":"O"},{"fullName":"Shulga S","lastName":"Shulga","firstName":"Sergiy","initials":"S"}]},"pubYear":"2026","abstractText":"<title>Abstract</title>  <p>Genome editing using CRISPR/Cas9 has become a powerful tool for genetic engineering of Saccharomyces cerevisiae, allowing for the rapid creation of strains with modified metabolic pathways. Multicopy integration of heterologous genes is often required to achieve sufficient expression levels, and δ-sites of the yeast genome are often used as targets due to the presence of numerous repetitive elements. However, simultaneous targeting of multiple δ-sites by CRISPR/Cas9 can result in significant DNA damage and reduced cell viability, limiting the effectiveness of this approach. This study describes an optimised strategy for CRISPR/Cas9-mediated multicopy integration into the δ-sites of the S. cerevisiae genome. Previously described approaches caused pronounced toxicity due to simultaneous targeting of multiple δ-elements. This toxicity likely stems from excessive DNA double-strand breaks generated by simultaneous cleavage across multiple genomic loci. To overcome this limitation, a modified approach combining inducible Cas9 expression with reduced plasmid copy number has been developed. This strategy provides more precise control of nuclease activity and reduces the burden of concomitant DNA damage. Using the optimised system, viable transformants with successful integration of donor DNA into δ-sites of the yeast genome were obtained. The proposed approach provides a practical basis for controlled multicopy genome engineering in S. cerevisiae and may facilitate the creation of engineered yeast strains for biotechnological applications.</p>","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Preprint"]},"bookOrReportDetails":{"publisher":"Research Square","yearOfPublication":2026},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-10919496/v1"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCreation":"2026-09-24","firstPublicationDate":"2026-09-23","firstIndexDate":"2026-09-24","versionList":{"version":[{"id":"PPR1325806","source":"PPR","versionNumber":1,"firstPublishDate":"2026-09-23","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["preprint"]},"hasEvaluations":"N"}]},"versionNumber":1,"hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42138085","source":"MED","pmid":"42138085","pmcid":"PMC13178663","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC131